          "The $72,500 purchase (about $652,000 in 1996 dollars) gave the twenty-five-year-old Rockefeller sole control of a refinery processing 500 barrels of crude daily, twice the capacity of its nearest Cleveland rival; the new firm was renamed Rockefeller and Andrews.",
          "Interwoven with the business narrative is Rockefeller's courtship of Laura Celestia \"Cettie\" Spelman, from a prominent, reform-minded Akron and Cleveland family whose parents were committed abolitionists whose home served as an Underground Railroad station.",
          "Rockefeller proposed to Cettie in early 1864 in what a family friend described as \"a business-like way,\" bought a $118 diamond engagement ring (a striking extravagance for him), and married her on September 8, 1864, in a small private ceremony at the Spelman home.",
