        youtube: "",
        principle: "Jensen codified Nvidia's culture around 'Speed of Light' (measure against physics, not competitors), relentless work hours, and public paranoia ('thirty days from going out of business'), then restructured engineering into a 'Three Teams, Two Seasons' model that let Nvidia ship a new chip every six months.",
