        principle: "The manifesto's most combative section names its opposition explicitly as bad ideas rather than bad people, then lists a specific roster: stagnation, statism and central planning, bureaucracy, regulatory capture and monopoly, unaccountable credentialed experts, speech control, utopian \"unconstrained vision\" thinking, the precautionary principle, de-growth and depopulation ideology, and Nietzsche's figure of the complacent \"Last Man.\"",
